.Dd 2026-05-30
.Dt NOMAD-FIX-KIWIX 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-fix-kiwix
.Nd manually run the Kiwix self-heal pass
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad fix-kiwix
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm nomad fix-kiwix
runs the Kiwix self-heal pass once, on demand.
This is the same logic a LaunchAgent runs automatically every 60 seconds, so
you rarely need it; use it when you want to force a check immediately rather
than wait for the next scheduled run.
.Pp
The self-heal script is silent and takes no action when Kiwix is healthy.
When it finds a partial or broken ZIM that is wedging the server, it moves
that file aside into the quarantine directory and restarts Kiwix so the
remaining archives stay available.
.Pp
.Nm nomad fix-kiwix
prints the Kiwix container state before and after the pass, the recent
self-heal action log, the final container state, whether Kiwix is responding
over HTTP, and the contents of the quarantine directory.
.Pp
It requires the self-heal script to be installed
.Pq run Xr nomad-install 1
and the
.Sy nomad_kiwix_server
container to exist
.Pq bring the stack up with Xr nomad-up 1 ,
or wait for the admin service to spawn Kiwix once a ZIM download finishes.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad fix-kiwix
Run the self-heal pass now and report Kiwix's state.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-clean 1 ,
.Xr nomad-zim 1
